abstract: >-
  Lean 4 verifies that the overlap supremum of a 9,408-cell rational step
  function is exactly U = 2462273619527794579322422405079 /
  6465103708838880000000000000000 < 0.38085601258978320592.
  Lean proves attainment at s = -571/1176, and an independent exact Python
  audit verifies that this maximizing shift is unique. The witness improves
  the November 25, 2026 Compute Substrate parent bound
  123113681346619/323255185441944 by more than 1.14531579911e-9.
  The Lean theorems witness_supremum_exact and continuous_upper_bound are
  unconditional. The proof uses pure kernel packed integer multiplication,
  zero sorry, zero native_decide, and only the standard axioms propext,
  Classical.choice, and Quot.sound. The proof declarations were replayed
  with leanchecker. In this archived v1.0.0 release, the discrete corollary
  assumes Swinnerton-Dyer's theorem, proved in Haugland (1996). White (2022),
  equation (1.1), gives the continuous objective.
  GPT-6.2 Astra and GPT-6.2 Sol assisted in Codex.
keywords:
  - Erdős Problem 36
  - minimum overlap
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
